 "ratioMeaning": "column differential / native differential, same language version and compiler family (lower is better; 1.00 = no overhead over native)",
 "spreadMeaning": "maxSpreadPct: largest (max - min) / median of I(n1) or I(n2) over the runs, percent (lower is better; 0 = bit-exact)",
 "lane": {
  "language": "java",
  "dockerfile": "languages/wasm/java/Dockerfile",
  "nativeImage": "lang-lab-wasm:java",
  "nativeRun": "/app/java/native/{b}",
  "nativeEnv": {},
  "nativeKind": "native",
  "wasmImage": "lang-lab-wasm:java",
  "wasmtimeRun": "/usr/local/bin/wasmtime run -C cache=n --allow-precompiled /app/java/wasm/{b}.cwasm",
  "nodeRun": "/usr/local/bin/node --predictable --single-threaded --single-threaded-gc --no-liftoff /opt/wasm/run-node.mjs /app/java/wasm/{b}.wasm",
  "wasmKind": "native",
  "wasmEnv": {
   "TOKIO_WORKER_THREADS": "1"
  },
  "versions": {
   "runtimeLabel": "TeaVM 0.13.1 (frozen release; its WASI backend was removed in 0.14.0). NOT the JVM: not comparable to the matrix Java cells",
   "teavm": "0.13.1 (teavm-cli sha256 eb31af75aaab678acaf01722bcf3c1f8b16de8dee488fc3e480272bc1a8afee1; full closure in languages/wasm/teavm/jars.lock)",
   "frontEnd": "javac --release 25 (JDK 25.0.4.1, Debian openjdk-25-jdk-headless; TeaVM 0.13.1 rejects class file major version 70, so the matrix Java 26 cannot be used)",
   "nativeBackend": "TeaVM -t C -O 3 --min-heap 32 --max-heap 512, all.c compiled by /opt/llvm/bin/clang 23.1.0 -O2 -lm",
   "wasmBackend": "TeaVM -t wasi -O 3 --min-heap 32 --max-heap 512, wasmtime 50.0.0 compile (AOT) / Node 26.5.0"
  },
  "transforms": [
   "none on the sources; the same class files (one front-end compile per benchmark) feed both TeaVM backends"
  ],
  "asymmetries": [
   "primary: the native column is TeaVM's C backend + LLVM clang -O2; the wasm column is TeaVM's own wasm emitter (no LLVM, no binaryen pass) + Cranelift, so the ratio mixes backend quality with the wasm cost",
   "TeaVM runtime and GC differ per backend: the C backend uses its C runtime (memory.c, glibc) and the wasi backend its own Java-written/wasm runtime with linear memory sized by --min-heap/--max-heap; same heap flags on both",
   "the wasm backend runs without wasm exception-handling instructions (--wasm-use-exceptions not set); the C backend uses its own mechanism",
   "front end is javac 25 not the matrix Java 26, and TeaVM replaces the JDK class library with its own classlib: no HotSpot, no JIT, no JVM GC anywhere",
   "TeaVM 0.13.1 output is not byte-reproducible: two builds of the same Dockerfile gave identical tak.wasm but a different bigint.wasm of the same size (cause not investigated)"
  ],
  "na": {},
  "columnRoles": {
   "native": "control",
   "wasmtime": "wasm",
   "node": "wasm"
  }
 },
